Subject: Cantor FILE_STREAM_INFO Pure Parser Decision

& [ResearchIdentity] is primary-source bound
  + [research_uuid] is 3cb0a9db-8ef4-4d3a-9102-e1c9f97eec3e
  + [captured_at] is 2026-07-30
  + [decision] is split pure chain parsing from later physical query and policy admission

@ [Microsoft_FILE_STREAM_INFO] https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winbase/ns-winbase-file_stream_info
@ [Microsoft_FSCC] https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/openspecs/windows_protocols/ms-fscc/f8762be6-3ab9-411e-a7d6-5cc68f70c78d

& [PrimaryFindings] are exact
  + NextEntryOffset is relative to the beginning of the current entry and zero on the last entry
  + StreamNameLength is bytes, not UTF-16 code units
  + StreamSize and StreamAllocationSize are signed 64-bit fields and stream size must be nonnegative
  + StreamName is non-NUL-terminated UTF-16 in ::$DATA or :name:$DATA form
  + each nonfinal entry is aligned to eight bytes
  + intervening alignment padding is ignored by receivers
  + support for named streams is filesystem-specific

& [ParserDecision] is stricter than transport
  + [exact_region] caller must supply only the successful returned byte region, not capacity
  + [empty] rejects because it cannot prove one complete information element
  + [terminal_tail] rejects unaccounted bytes after the final name
  + [limits] are caller-supplied and checked before allocation or release
  + [no_admission] named stream rejection and kind-specific default-stream truth remain separate policy

& [Nonclaim] is explicit
  - parser success does not prove an API call, complete enumeration, stream support, physical file, or admissible topology
